From f22424314940e366f1a5e326041483a7c6c06234 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exploitizm <351399878+exploitizm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:33:57 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] ac/nir/ngg: mesh shaders get the GFX10 workaround for
 fully culled workgroups

GFX10 hangs when an NGG workgroup allocates no primitive
(has_ngg_fully_culled_bug); the vertex and geometry shader paths export a
culled primitive instead, but the mesh shader path passed false, as mesh
shaders upstream run only on GFX10.3 and later. The PS5's GPU is GFX10 and
runs them, and a mesh workgroup that culls all its primitives then hangs it:
its waves end, but the end-of-pipe event after the draw never comes.

Ocarina of Time (on Eden) hit it at its first task+mesh draws: in the stall
dump, the mesh waves of the stuck draw had finished (a VS_PARTIAL_FLUSH and a
marker behind it passed) and the GPU waited on the end-of-pipe fence.
---
 src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c b/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c
index 1809ccb..053e1b3 100644
--- a/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/nir/ac_nir_lower_ngg_mesh.c
@@ -721,7 +721,11 @@ ms_alloc_vertices_and_primitives(nir_builder *b, nir_def *num_vtx, nir_def *num_
       num_prm = ms_part_prims(b, num_prm, s);
       num_vtx = nir_imul_imm(b, num_prm, s->vertices_per_prim);
    }
-   ac_nir_ngg_alloc_vertices_and_primitives(b, num_vtx, num_prm, false);
+   /* GFX10 hangs when a workgroup allocates no primitive: such a workgroup
+    * exports a culled one instead, as the other NGG stages do. Mesh shaders
+    * meet it on GFX10 when a workgroup culls all its primitives.
+    */
+   ac_nir_ngg_alloc_vertices_and_primitives(b, num_vtx, num_prm, s->ac->has_ngg_fully_culled_bug);
 }
 
 static void
